  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 346 AM CDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nWe continue to see weak ridging across the Southern CONUS with \nsouthwest mid-lvl flow across the Central Plains. This will allow a \nsubtle shortwave trough to lift across the area early today. An\nincrease in mid-lvl cloudiness is anticipated with a few \nsprinkles possible, although a plethora of dry air in the sub \ncloud layer should result in evaporation/sublimation with little\nif anything reaching the sfc. This pattern will remain \nunchanged as we move into Tue as another subtle shortwave trough\napproaches from the SW bringing an increase in mid-lvl clouds \nand perhaps a few sprinkles, although most locations are \nexpected to remain dry. Seasonably mild temperatures are \nanticipated through Tue.\n\nThe mid/upper ridge is progged to amplify over the Central Plains \nWed-Thu resulting in rising temperatures across the area with highs \nclimbing into the mid and upper 70s. A mid/upper trough is progged \nto build into the Rockies late in the week before emerging over the \nCentral and Northern Plains as we move into the weekend. Some modest \npops were maintained across much of the area but we continue to see \nsome differences in how quickly this system moves over the area \nleading to some timing uncertainty. Seasonably mild temperatures are \nexpected to persist over the weekend and in the wake of this system \nas we move into early next week.",
